113: We conducted the network training described in section 3.1 of the main text with AdamW optimizer (with the parameters suggested in the original RoBERTa paper: β 1 = 0 . 9 , β 2 = 0 . 98 , ε = 10 − 6 and weight decay of 0.01), with batch sizes of 128 or 256 (depending on model size) and sequences of 256 tokens each. We started with pretrained RoBERTA-base weights from the HuggingFace Transformers repository 4 , and continued training them on the MLM task with masking probability of 15%, where each masked token had a probability of 80% of being replaced with the special [ MASK ] token, 10% of being replaced with a random token and 10% of being kept the same. The data used for this phase of training was created using the four different procedures described in section 3.1. After the training was ﬁnished, we evaluated the models’ performance using the SentEval kit.
